The root problem with conventional currency is all the trust that's required to make it work.

The root problem with verifying is all the skill and work that's required to make it happen.

Optimistically, as LLMs become cheaper &amp; better, they can act as our verification agents.

@grace_za It's trust all the way down, but you can minimize trust across any given piece of software by having a variety of software perform the same function and cross-check each other.

@ZigarioPepers You can minimize trust across any given piece of software by having a variety of different software perform the same function and cross-check each other.

@SBS222444 It's trust all the way down, but you can minimize trust across any given piece of software by having a variety of software perform the same function and cross-check each other. Thus, robust harnesses will wield multiple models to distribute trust.

